---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import CentredImage from "../../components/CentredImage.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import inspector from "../../img/web/inspector.png"
import stack_1 from "../../img/web/stack-1.jpg"
import stack_2 from "../../img/web/stack-2.jpg"
import stack_3 from "../../img/web/stack-3.jpg"
import stack_gradient from "../../img/web/stack-gradient.jpg"
---
<Slide t1="More React">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Messing around with the DOM</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="The DOM">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">The DOM (Document Object Model) is the browser's <em>internal representation</em>
            of a web page</li>
        <li class="fragment">Use <code>Inspect</code> in your web browser to see it</li>
        <li class="fragment">It is displayed as HTML (with CSS classes, styles etc.)</li>
        <li class="fragment">It is dynamic, and libraries like jQuery, React, Vue, Svelte etc. can change it</li>
        <li class="fragment">It generally diverges from the original HTML delivered to the browser</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide>
    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <Image
            src={ inspector }
            alt="DOM Inspector"
            height="600"
            width="800" />
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide>
    <ul>
        <li>In React (in Astro), we embedded <em>components</em> into our HTML source</li>
    </ul>

    <CodeBlock lang="html" height="175px">
            { `
<Layout>
    <h1>Stack Some Boxes</h1>
    <StackerComponent client:only />
</Layout>
            `.trim() }
    </CodeBlock>
</Slide>

<Slide>
    <ul>
        <li>We <em>implement</em> the components in JavaScript, but can refer to other
            components (JSX)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="flex">
        <div class="text-sm-2">
            <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="200px">
                { `
function OneBox({ pos }) {
    return <div key={pos}
                style={ {backgroundColor: "red",
                         border: "3px solid black",
                         margin: "5px",
                         width: "200px",
                         height: "25px"} } />
}
                `.trim() }
            </CodeBlock>
        </div>

        <div class="text-sm-2">
            <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="350px">
                { `
export default function StackerComponent() {
    const [boxes, setBoxes] = useState([])

    function addBox() {
        setBoxes([      // Replace the entire set of boxes.
            ...boxes,
            OneBox({pos: boxes.length})
        ])
    }

    return (
        <>
            { boxes }
            <div><button
                type="button"
                onClick={ addBox }>Add a box</button></div>
        </>
    )
}
                `.trim() }
            </CodeBlock>
        </div>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Box Stacking">
    <div class="columns-3">
        {
            [stack_1, stack_2, stack_3].map(p => (
                <CentredImage
                    src={ p }
                    size={ [175, 200 ] }
                />
            ))
        }
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="State Variables">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">The React <em>hook</em> <code>useState</code> creates state variables inside components</li>
        <li class="fragment">Change the state variable, and the page updates to reflect the new value</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t1="Exercises">
    <ul class="text-sm-1">
        <li class="fragment">How would you randomise the appearance of the boxes?</li>

        <ul class="fragment">
            <li>Colour (or harder: gradient!)</li>
            <li>Shape</li>
            <li>Position</li>
        </ul>

        <li class="fragment">What other actions could you add?</li>

        <ul class="fragment">
            <li>Clear</li>
            <li>Remove last</li>
            <li>Shuffle</li>
        </ul>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Randomness">
    <div class="columns-2">
        <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ stack_gradient }
                alt="React Stack Gradient"
                height="200"
                width="175" />
        </div>

        <ul>
            <li>Random size (width, height)</li>
            <li>Random colour hue</li>
            <li>Random border radius</li>
            <li>Random lightness (with gradient)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</Slide>
